{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated","id":1552052,"title":"The Arcanum (Updated)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-04T02:24:13-07:00","id":1552052,"title":"The Arcanum (Updated)","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I seem to be very much in the minority in that I\u2019m fond of the Arcanum. I even had a Mage character some years ago whose concept was \u201cthe first Awakened member of the Arcanum.\u201d They\u2019re punching above their weight class in just managing to <b><i>survive</i></b> the attention of the various supernatural factions in the World of Darkness. But they\u2019re not just surviving, they\u2019re thriving. Slowly but surely, they\u2019re putting together an increasingly clear picture of the supernatural truth of the world. So, I can\u2019t help but root for these underdogs who are underestimated by nearly everyone.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, there\u2019s no single sourcebook for them. They\u2019re in bits and pieces all over the place, so trying to assemble a coherent picture of them was an exercise in research (and purchasing numerous sourcebooks hoping to find even a further tidbit of information about them). This is an excerpt from my House Rules Document, which provides a unified overview of the Arcanum as I best envision them.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>The Nine Founders</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">These are unchanged from canon. It\u2019s still not known just who (or what) Benjamen Holmscroft really was. He\u2019s almost certainly still out there somewhere, however.</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Benjamen Holmscroft, of London</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Jebediah Brown, of London</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Roger Corwin, of Salisbury</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Peter Harker, of London</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Stewart Heath, of Manchester</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Winthrop Murray, of Kent</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Liam McPhee, of Dublin</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Jonathan Kelvin, of Boston, U.S.A.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Massimo Linarelli, of Rome, Italy</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Structure</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In canon, their structure seems to vary a bit by which book you read. As such, after reading all of sourcebooks that deal with the Arcanum, I present this simplified organizational structure, which is (roughly) modeled after a typical university.</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">At the top is the Board of Governors\u2026otherwise known as the White Monks. Their identity is a closely-guarded secret and they\u2019re the ones who appoint each Chancellor. A small and secret group of dissidents who style themselves \u201cThe Red Monks\u201d oppose them.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The \u201cCEO position\u201d is the Chancellor, who has global authority over all Chapter Houses.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A Director is the head of a Chapter House.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A Dean is the head of a College (these are divisions of interest and study of a particular subject; e.g., ghosts, vampires, magic, history, etc.).</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A Headmaster (or Headmistress) is the head of a Colony. They\u2019re promoted to Director if the Colony graduates to full Chapter House status.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All of the Chapter Houses report directly to the Foundation House in the UK. Disregard all references in canon books to a \u201cprimary\u201d Chapter House for a given geographical region. That said, when a Chapter House <b><i>does</i></b> communicate with the \u201chome office,\u201d they\u2019re not likely to get through directly to the Chancellor unless it\u2019s a matter of great importance. In short, the \u201cmiddle managers\u201d are all at the Foundation House so as to better coordinate with each other and the Chancellor about Arcanum business as a whole.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Another change is that they\u2019ve become a bit more \u201cfamily friendly\u201d in recent years. That is to say, they\u2019ve noticed that the few kids raised \u201cin house\u201d by Arcanum parents have typically gone on to become accomplished members themselves. Accordingly, they now encourage prospective parents to raise their children within the organization in order to \u201cpromote from within.\u201d There are also unofficial rewards for Arcanum couples who have children in order to further facilitate this. This is ameliorating their declining membership problem, but at the cost of making them a more insular society. [The Social Flaw: <a href=\"https://vampiremagehunter.proboards.com/thread/8/list-merits-flaws\" target=\"_blank\">Isolated Upbringing</a> is slowly becoming more common among Arcanum members.]</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Bibliography</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Mage: The Ascension</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">M20 \u2013 Inside the Chapter House</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">M20 \u2013 Paths of Power</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">M20 \u2013 Sorcerer</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mage Chronicles \u2013 Volume 2 (Halls of the Arcanum)<br /> Sorcerer \u2013 The Hedge Wizard's Handbook</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Vampire: The Masquerade</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">V20 \u2013 20<sup>th</sup> Anniversary Edition (Core Book)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">V20 \u2013 The Hunters Hunted II</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">V5 \u2013 Second Inquisition</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Encyclopaedia Vampirica</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">MET Laws of the Hunt Revised Edition</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Hunters Hunted</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Inquisition</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Wraith: The Oblivion</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Wraith 20 \u2013 World of Darkness: Ghost Hunters</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Wraith 20 \u2013 World of Darkness: Paranormal Investigator\u2019s Handbook</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Hunter: The Reckoning</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">First Contact</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>World of Darkness \u2013 Other</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mummy \u2013 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Websites</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"http://mage.gearsonline.net/anders/misc/setting/arcanum.html\" target=\"_blank\">Arcanum in London</a> (Anders Mage Page)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>YouTube</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=14z0mttRH-o\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Podcast \u2013 Halls of the Arcanum</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bKpjGDj5o_k\" target=\"_blank\">Halls of the Arcanum OST</a></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Books</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talamasca\" target=\"_blank\">Talamasca</a> from Anne Rice\u2019s <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Vampire_Chronicles\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire Chronicles</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lives_of_the_Mayfair_Witches\" target=\"_blank\">Lives of the Mayfair Witches</a>.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>TV and Films</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I can also recommend watching <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poltergeist%3A_The_Legacy\" target=\"_blank\">Poltergeist: The Legacy</a>, which could be called \u201cArcanum: The TV Series.\u201d</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28819,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","user":"Arcanum Scholar","date":". 07-06-2025, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T03:48:57-07:00","id":1552053,"title":"","content":"The Arcanum is based on the Talamasca from the Anne Rice chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T15:22:33-07:00","id":1552062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552053#post1552053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arcanum is based on the Talamasca from the Anne Rice chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should add that to the bibliography section. It's been a long time since I read any Anne Rice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T18:09:37-07:00","id":1552065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552053#post1552053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arcanum is based on the Talamasca from the Anne Rice chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they first appeared in 1st edition Vampire and The Hunters Hunted, they pretty much were the Talamasca with a different name.<br /> <br /> IIRC, <b>The Witching Hour</b> was the first of Rice's books to feature the Talamasca. I know there is a recent TV adaptation, but I am blanking on the name. (<i>The Mayfair Witches</i>?)<br /> <br /> I also recommend the 1999 film <b>The Ninth Gate</b>, about a specialist in rare books looking for a tome on demonology. It is a loose adaptation of Arturo P\u00e9rez-Reverte's novel <b>The Club Dumos</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T07:14:15-07:00","id":1552072,"title":"","content":"It's perhaps worth noting that the Arcanum outright appears in the list of Affiliations in M20 Sorcerer. It may indicate a further shift towards a more 'practical' approach, something older books have stated the Order of Hermes was waiting for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T01:44:55-07:00","id":1552096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552072#post1552072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's perhaps worth noting that the Arcanum outright appears in the list of Affiliations in M20 Sorcerer. It may indicate a further shift towards a more 'practical' approach, something older books have stated the Order of Hermes was waiting for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly can't believe I missed adding those. [slaps self upside head] I've updated the Bibliography section again.<br /> <br /> If anyone else knows of any other mentions of the Arcanum in World of Darkness sourcebooks I haven't listed, please let me know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T09:47:26-07:00","id":1552104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated#post1552052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=Calibri]I seem to be very much in the minority in that I\u2019m fond of the Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one reason why the Arcanum is not heavily used is that STs don't know what purpose it could serve in their chronicles and therefore how Arcanum characters can be used. Every time it gets mentioned, there is always a line about how this organization should be avoided because of the Masquerade, Veil, Protocols, etc. Therefore, PCs need to avoid them. It's very much like a plot using hunters, but without any physical danger. There's only so much you can do with such a plot. Of course, PCs could always choose to disregard these prohibitions and make contact, but what would be the corresponding reward versus the danger of the appropriate authorities (archons, sept elders, masters, etc.) punishing you for it? The risk/reward ratio isn't enough.<br /> <br /> Contrast to the Talamasca which is the most similar organization in Anne Rice's books. Their members get involved ALL the time despite <i>their</i> organization (not those of vampires or witches) telling its operatives not to do so. They also tend to be very useful to the protagonists, providing all sorts of information (exposition) and helping them in ways.<br /> <br /> So if you want the Arcanum to be useful in your chronicle (the PCs interact with its members), you need to come up with a way to get past this block. Have Arcanum scholars want to contact PCs (or at least interact with in certain social circles). That's fairly easy. The more difficult thing is internal considerations for your supernatural splat so that such contact is not something that will get your PC killed.<br /> <br /> So instead of a blanket prohibition against contact, instead it should be something more like, &quot;Of all the mortals/kine/flock/sleepers/etc. you may get involved with, interaction with the Arcanum may be the least problematic because 1) they already know we exist, and 2) they are sworn not to reveal it to outsiders. Interaction should still be considered dangerous, but not inherently a breach of the Masquerade/Veil/Protocols/etc. Be wary and use common sense.&quot;<br /> <br /> That opens up more possibilities for interaction. Arcanum members can then become part of a character's Backgrounds like Allies or Contacts. For STs, they could make a good &quot;neutral&quot; scholar for whatever plot exposition is needed. Why go to the treacherous Tremere for information on the Ritual of the Bitter Rose when an NPC of the Arcanum could provide that information? Need guidance on dealing with characters of another splat? Use the Arcanum as a way for the PCs to learn that. Then at some point once the PCs owe an Arcanum scholar for past help, that character can be used to introduce new plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T11:37:46-07:00","id":1552206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552104#post1552104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one reason why the Arcanum is not heavily used is that STs don't know what purpose it could serve in their chronicles and therefore how Arcanum characters can be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these ideas.<br /> <br /> In my case, my WoD group is also big into Call of Cthulhu. Most of the time, they prefer Vampire, leaving me the lone Mage holdout. But I was once able to talk them into a short all-Arcanum campaign, pitching it as &quot;like Call of Cthulhu, but in the World of Darkness.&quot; So, that's a possibility if you have CoC players.<br /> <br /> But I like the more interaction idea. Though that does mean the Arcanum's knowledge base would grow rapidly. In canon, you can see that they've uncovered <i><b>some </b></i>truths, but also come to some wrong conclusions as they're only seeing part of the picture. More contact with the various supernaturals means that those wrong conclusions will get corrected and they'll sooner rather than later assemble a more full and accurate view of what's going on in the World of Darkness. What happens next is anybody's guess. Holmscroft and Murray are still out there (both of them are probably Cabiri) and one wonder's how much control they still have of the organization...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28819,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","user":"Arcanum Scholar","date":". 07-08-2025, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T14:16:20-07:00","id":1552214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552206#post1552206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I like the more interaction idea. Though that does mean the Arcanum's knowledge base would grow rapidly. In canon, you can see that they've uncovered <i><b>some </b></i>truths, but also come to some wrong conclusions as they're only seeing part of the picture. More contact with the various supernaturals means that those wrong conclusions will get corrected and they'll sooner rather than later assemble a more full and accurate view of what's going on the World of Darkness. What happens next is anybody's guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that the Arcanum should probably &quot;know&quot; the high level basics of vampire as it is in the original 2e hardcover corebook. They &quot;know&quot; the main clans and a rough description of each akin to their two page blurb. They know the two main sects as briefly described in the corebook (which confuses the Black Hand with the Sabbat). They have a general knowledge of the major Disciplines. Anything found in the Players Guides, Clanbooks, and other sourcebooks is mostly out of scope unless you, as the ST, wants them to know it specifically.<br /> <br /> I would stress that the Arcanum's job to figure things out is MUCH, MUCH harder than what we as players know. Players know what is objectively true from the sourcebooks we read. The Arcanum must shift through a lot of bullshit, personal bias, and the incomplete information provided to them in whatever capacity from any actual contacts. They won't accept things uncritically. They need to piece things together themselves. <br /> <br /> Players tend to assume a LOT more knowledge for their characters than they should because once they read something in a sourcebook, they know it. Even if there is no reason their character should know. Just reflect on how much characters were not expected to know in the original Chicago By Night compared to now. Basic things like that primogen existed, who served the Prince, the very concept of diablerie, and other information were &quot;secrets&quot; not known to every character.<br /> <br /> This is how I would handle certain things.<br /> <br /> In the rare chances of an Arcanum scholar interviewing vampires, they are not going to be info dumped on everything in the corebook or the White Wolf Wiki. They are scholars who need to verify all details and try to be as objective as possible. They are going to be critical with every piece of information given. How much time will any individual vampire really give an Arcanum scholar? Vampires have their own agendas, time restrictions, and interest.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, how much does any vampire character actually &quot;know&quot;? Not only in the sense of the above example with &quot;secrets&quot;, but in the sense of &quot;I was there. I am a witness.&quot; versus &quot;This is what I was told by another vampire.&quot; The first makes it a primary source. The other is a secondary source which is much less useful.<br /> <br /> What does a vampire gain from talking to the Arcanum? For most, it would be nothing which means they would have no interest in telling the Arcanum anything. Each vampire who does has their own agenda for doing so. It's likely not to be nice and provide this group of mortals free information in the interest of truth and justice.<br /> <br /> Also, the Arcanum expects vampires to be liars. Not only may other vampires have lied to the vampire being interviewed, the vampire being interviewed could be lying. Everything needs to be taken with a grain of salt and compared against other verifiable information. Maybe they had one informant who was secretly an archon, and he fed them complete misinformation that only seems true. Not all vampire informants are equally credible. The Arcanum needs to be equally skilled in spycraft as it is in scholarship.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum will also be wanting specific, objective information which they can use to form the basis of their <i>own</i> scholarly opinions. They won't want summaries of events that the vampire wasn't part of. They will be much more interested in a vampire reciting his own lineage than some eighth hand story about the Anarch Revolt. Doesn't mean they won't tape record everything, but that story is of dubious scholastic value even if they hear it repeated by multiple people. (Think of how many people &quot;know&quot; that the Europeans thought the world was flat before Columbus. That is totally untrue. They knew the world was round, but had disputes on its exact size. That &quot;knowledge&quot; is a result of Washington Irving's &quot;biography&quot; of Christopher Columbus and became popular knowledge. The Arcanum will know simply because many people report the same story, it doesn't make it true.) The petty details - which are usually completely ignored by PCs because they aren't &quot;fun&quot; to bring up during the game - will be far more important because those petty details is what that vampire actually knows as a witness.<br /> <br /> Arcanum scholars also need to be very protective of themselves and of their &quot;informers&quot;. Things can easily grow wrong. Vampires are very dangerous creatures. In canon, the first time they made contact with a vampire, it lead to the destruction of the Boston chapterhouse. There is going to be a lot of intrigue involved. Likewise there is still some danger to the vampire informant even if this isn't an instant kill situation. Individual archons, princes, or random vampires may not like any Kindred telling them anything. There should still be some level of danger. It's just the exact extent in that domain is up to the ST. (And different splats may even be worse.)<br /> <br /> Lastly, remember the total number of vampire &quot;informants&quot; all depends on you, the ST. Maybe they only had four vampires in history willing to tell them something other than the one PC in your chronicle who is willing to talk. Or maybe they had twenty vampires talking to them, but sixteen knew almost nothing valuable. After talking with one Anarch, they had to completely revisit all the information they had previously &quot;known&quot; was &quot;true&quot; about the Camarilla. It should be rare enough that any time a PC wishes to become involved in the Arcanum that should be a BIG opportunity for the Arcanum.<br /> <br /> When portraying such Arcanum characters in the games, you should be taking into consideration how scholars like this operate and what kind of information they really want. Roleplay them challenging the PC(s) actual knowledge, as opposed to what they think they know. (This might be a good way to get players to question how much their character actually &quot;knows&quot;.) They are going to act like a combination of scholars, spy handlers, journalists, police detectives, and prosecutors towards the PC(s). Even if they act nice and credulous to the PC(s) to keep them happy and talking, they are going to be a lot more skeptical and objective in their reports to the Arcanum itself.<br /> <br /> The final extent of the Arcanum's knowledge is up to the ST, but I would argue they would probably &quot;know&quot; a lot less than you might expect them to know even in a scenario where they do have more interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T17:51:01-07:00","id":1552219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552214#post1552214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The final extent of the Arcanum's knowledge is up to the ST, but I would argue they would probably &quot;know&quot; a lot less than you might expect them to know even in a scenario where they do have more interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to agree with your reasoning, that said, their biggest problem in canon is that the various supernaturals of the world aren't very talkative around them. If that changed, and interactions became a more common occurrence, their knowledge can only increase. I get what you're saying about having to sift useful information out of half-truths, personal biases, and outright lies, but still, if they talk to enough supernaturals it helps them cut closer to the truth. So, the real question is...how much interaction would they be getting? If &quot;Interview With the Vampire&quot; is practically a weekly event, then within a decade they'll know a lot more than either the Camarilla or the Sabbat would like them to.<br /> <br /> And then one wonders if they can find any chatty mages or werewolves...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T19:17:37-07:00","id":1552221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552214#post1552214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, remember the total number of vampire &quot;informants&quot; all depends on you, the ST. Maybe they only had four vampires in history willing to tell them something other than the one PC in your chronicle who is willing to talk. Or maybe they had twenty vampires talking to them, but sixteen knew almost nothing valuable. After talking with one Anarch, they had to completely revisit all the information they had previously &quot;known&quot; was &quot;true&quot; about the Camarilla. It should be rare enough that any time a PC wishes to become involved in the Arcanum that should be a BIG opportunity for the Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This situation actually holds up even if they talked to a lot of vampires through the years.<br /> <br /> Most of the information gleaned is probably redundant, and that's truer the more people they ask. Most Vampires can't really say a lot about whatever happened beyond their city or their personal experiences. Is the Camarilla even real? Is really any undead in the city more than a century old?<br /> <br /> In a sense the Arcanum, by its own nature, is actually likely to know more about some things than most vampires (not most players), but that isn't to say much. Most vampires don't really know as much as we think (much less with any reliability).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552052-the-arcanum-updated?p=1552219#post1552219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that changed, and interactions became a more common occurrence, their knowledge can only increase. I get what you're saying about having to sift useful information out of half-truths, personal biases, and outright lies, but still, if they talk to enough supernaturals it helps them cut closer to the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but not as much, and definitely not as fast.<br /> <br /> Everything told about Vampires still holds about everyone else: they're unreliable. <b><i>Extremely</i></b> unreliable. It comes back again to how we perceive the lore, because we know for sure most truths, but the characters don't.<br /> <br /> Not only that, keep in mind that they get contradicting information, and that new data may put old data in check. How much the Arcanum knows for sure is probably very little, and most other things are just suppositions and unreliable data. It may take years, even decades, to confirm anything at all.<br /> <br /> And more talkative supernaturals don't change that as much. Again, most of what they say will be redundant, on top of unverified, plus contradictions. What can a Mage really reveal about Vampires that the Arcanum will have any particular reason to believe? Or a Garou, or Changeling?<br /> <br /> Finally, most lore known through vampiric society is relatively innocuous from the perspective of the big secrets of the movers and shakers. If half the vampires in a city know something, it can hardly be called a secret anymore. The Camarilla and the Sabbat are more concerned with plots that very few vampires have any clue about. At most they would be worried about the Masquerade, but the Arcanum isn't really a big threat to it (they already know things, and they're not sharing with hunters or society at large).<br /> <br /> How much the Arcanum will be a problem in a given area is much more dependent on their local relationships to other supernaturals, and they may be either a nuisance or a resource, depending on how much they're able to talk about others (or <b>with</b> others).<br /> <br /> The most that can happen with a more integrated Arcanum is that they'll have a better grasp of the current events in an area. They wouldn't know many actual secrets, but may know what's being talked in the streets, even if it isn't their main concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}